Steam Enhanced, compat/hltb-for-steam/hltb-for-steam.js: the How Long To Beat card asks the Arkada
plugin first, then the HLTB plugins it knew.

Why. Arkada does what the HLTB for Steam plugin did (plugin/backend/arkada_hltb.lua): its backend
answers GetHltbData with the same arguments and the same reply. The card only knew the names
hltb-for-steam and hltb-for-millennium, so with Arkada alone it stayed empty.

What. findHltbBackend tries "arkada", then the plugin it would have tried, then the other one, and
takes the first that answers. While Arkada's setting «Время прохождения» is off its backend answers
{ success: false, error: "off" } at once, so the card goes on to the HLTB plugins as before. The
card's markup, its data and its refresh are not changed.

--- a/compat/hltb-for-steam/hltb-for-steam.js
+++ b/compat/hltb-for-steam/hltb-for-steam.js
@@ -83,15 +83,20 @@
